# Cloud environment.json alignment

Obsidian plugin Cloud Agents use a **shared pointer** in `.cursor/environment.json`. Install/start scripts live only in **`obsidian-plugin-development`**; plugin repos must not copy `env-install.sh` / `env-start.sh` into their trees.

## Required contract

| Field | Rule |
| --- | --- |
| `install` | `bash .cursor/cloud-bootstrap.sh install` |
| `start` | `bash .cursor/cloud-bootstrap.sh start` |
| `repositoryDependencies` | Must list **every** checkout `env-install.sh` expects under `/agent/repos/`, including the orchestrator |

**Canonical `repositoryDependencies` (keep this set in sync everywhere the pointer is used):**

1. `github.com/adrianghnguyen/obsidian-plugin-development` — orchestrator; **required** for token scope and non-bootstrap agent layouts. `cloud-bootstrap.sh` symlinks `/workspace` when this repo is primary.
2. `github.com/adrianghnguyen/obsidian-agent-client`
3. `github.com/adrianghnguyen/obsidian-seek`
4. `github.com/adrianghnguyen/whisper-obsidian-plugin`
5. `github.com/adrianghnguyen/obsidian-book-search-plugin` — optional at install time; keep listed for token scope and parity.

Adding or removing a sibling plugin from the E2E bundle: update `env-install.sh` in **obsidian-plugin-development** first, then mirror the same `repositoryDependencies` list in every repo’s `.cursor/environment.json`.

## Cross-repo sync

These repos intentionally share the same pointer on `main` (names may differ; content must match):

- `adrianghnguyen/obsidian-plugin-development` (script source of truth)
- `adrianghnguyen/Obsidian-Seek`
- `adrianghnguyen/obsidian-seek`
- `adrianghnguyen/whisper-obsidian-plugin`
- `adrianghnguyen/obsidian-agent-client`
- `adrianghnguyen/obsidian-book-search-plugin` (when part of the bundle)

When you change `.cursor/environment.json` in one repo, **apply the identical JSON** to the others in the same change cycle (separate PRs per repo are fine; do not leave one repo with a stale dependency list).

## Agent checklist

1. Read `.cursor/environment.json` and confirm the orchestrator repo is in `repositoryDependencies`.
2. If editing dependencies or install/start paths, diff against obsidian-plugin-development `main` and sync sibling repos.
3. After merge to the repo tied to the Cloud environment dashboard, recommend a **draft environment build** and confirm logs pass `env-install.sh` (not `No such file or directory`) and agent boot runs `env-start.sh` (`/tmp/cursor/start-user/start-user.log`).

See `AGENTS.md` § Cursor Cloud environment and obsidian-plugin-development `scripts/cloud-e2e/GETTING-STARTED.md`.
